{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00341 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Cetirizine, a second-generation antihistamine, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Vasomotor Rhinitis through a series of off-label and indicated relationships. The evidence suggests that Cetirizine may contribute to Vasomotor Rhinitis via its role in inducing Atopic Eczema or Dermatitis, which in turn are linked to Tranilast, a drug that is indicated for Vasomotor Rhinitis. This chain of relationships implies a potential mechanistic pathway where Cetirizine, through its off-label use, may influence inflammatory processes that are associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis. The presence of multiple pathways involving different intermediate entities, such as Atopic Eczema and Papillary Conjunctivitis, further supports the idea that Cetirizine could have a broader impact on inflammatory or allergic responses that contribute to the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Cetirizine may exert a modulatory effect on the inflammatory cascade, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
